  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN. You can perform the following operation on it any number of times (possibly, zero):\n\n\nChoose any two distinct indices iii and jjj (1≤i,j≤N1\\leq i , j \\leq N1≤i,j≤N and i≠ji \\neq ji=j), and multiply both AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​ by −1-1−1.\n\nThat is, set AiA_iAi​ to −Ai-A_i−Ai​, and also AjA_jAj​ to −Aj-A_j−Aj​.\nFind the **maximum** possible sum of the array AAA after performing this operation several times.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN — the number of elements in AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible sum of AAA after several operations.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "−105≤Ai≤105-10^5 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^5−105≤Ai​≤105",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 4⋅1054\\cdot 10^54⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 \n1 0 3 3\n5\n-3 4 6 2 -1\n3\n-1 3 4",
        "output": "7\n16\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The sum of the array is 777, which is the best we can do. No operations are needed.\nTest case 222: Consider the following operation:\n\nChoose i=1i = 1i=1 and j=5j = 5j=5. The array becomes [3,4,6,2,1][3, 4, 6, 2, 1][3,4,6,2,1].\nIts sum is now 161616, which is the maximum possible."
      }
    ]
  },
